    basic: "Save your Aces. An Ace is your 'get out of jail free' card when you don't have the current suit. Don't play it too early unless you can switch the suit to one where you have a long sequence.",
    intermediate: "Stacking Mastery: If you have two 2s and a 3, wait until someone plays a 2 on YOU. Stack your 2s back at them to force them (or the next person) to draw 7 cards. This is the primary way to win a 'losing' game.",
    advanced: "The 'Seven-Stop' Defense: If you suspect the player before you is about to play a 'Draw 5' King, hold your 7 of any suit. It is the only way to nullify a high-draw penalty and seize the lead.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Count the 2s and 3s. If all four 2s are played, the 'Draw' danger is significantly reduced.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you holding a 5, check if your house rules allow 'Multi-5' discarding (playing multiple 5s in one turn).",
